\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we formulate proposed and accepted updates}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{optimization}

\p{We formulate an update proposal so that a gate may reject a computed
gradient without pretending that no computation occurred. The DGG definition
in \ref{ftip-005A} supplies the motivating pre-optimizer discard operation.
Other protocols may inspect held-out loss, divergence, or resource limits.}

\p{The generic proposal interface does not transfer DGG's empirical detector
to those other diagnostics. Each gate needs its own assumptions and
calibration evidence.}
